 "result": "The session cookie uses a tagged JSON scheme: non-JSON types are wrapped in a one-key dict on the way out and unwrapped on the way back in.\n\n- **`TypedCookieSerializer`** (`src/tessel/json/tag.py:219`) is the serializer. `tag()` (L289) walks a value and runs it through the first registered tag whose `check()` matches. `untag()` (L297) reverses that.\n- **`TypeMarker`** (`tag.py:60`) is the base class for the tags. Each subclass implements `check`, `to_json` and `to_python`:\n  - `TagTuple` (L133): tuple ↔ list.\n  - `TagBytes` (L159): bytes ↔ base64 string.\n  - `TagDateTime` (L205): datetime ↔ HTTP-date string.\n  - `TagMarkup`, `TagUUID`, `PassDict`, `PassList`: the other built-in tags.\n- **`TagDict`** (`tag.py:93`) handles dicts that already look like a tag (a single key that's a tag key). It escapes them so they aren't misread on the way back.\n- **`SecureCookieSessionInterface`** (`src/tessel/sessions.py:300`) sets `serializer = session_json_serializer` (L273, a `TypedCookieSerializer()` instance). `make_signer` (L303) builds an itsdangerous `URLSafeTimedSerializer` with it, so the cookie is tagged JSON, then signed.",
